  "narrative": "I use the controller's signed convention: for direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has the more negative, stronger-dependency composite score in the claimed direction; for direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has the less negative, weaker-dependency score in the claimed direction. H16 is reassessed at its response deadline. PTEN loss versus intact among screen-quality-eligible lines gives discovery R15 +0.217 [0.117, 0.317] and validation R26 +0.251 [0.112, 0.390]. Both point estimates exceed the 0.15-unit threshold in the stronger-dependency direction and replicate the same direction; together with accepted specificity checks H42 and H45, this supports PTEN loss as a dataset-specific marker association with moderately stronger negative dependency. The validation lower bound remains below threshold, so I keep the overall investigation active and do not treat the context-specific checks as separately established. H61 is the key CDKN2A follow-up: in high-quality TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact, SMARCA4-intact lines, discovery R47 is +0.172 [0.085, 0.259] and independent validation R53 is +0.184 [0.060, 0.308]. The point estimates consistently exceed the threshold in the claimed stronger-dependency direction, so I accept this as a modest, context-specific dataset association: CDKN2A loss is associated with more negative composite dependency in a cleaner co-intact high-quality subgroup. However, the validation interval lower bound is still below threshold, so I do not claim that the effect is precisely localized away from the threshold, and I do not generalize this to all lines. Consequently, H19, the overall CDKN2A main effect in screen-quality-eligible lines, is rejected and closed: R18 is +0.144 [0.060, 0.228], with a point estimate below the practical threshold, and the separate high-quality overall check H46 was also below threshold. The clean H61 subgroup result suggests a CDKN2A association in a restricted genomic background, not a robust overall main effect. Overall supported core: SMARCA4 loss is the strongest accepted association, with discovery and validation far above threshold and robust co-occurrence and direct subtype/phenotype checks. TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are accepted associations with weaker dependency, supported by high-quality or validated contrasts and several co-occurrence and stemness context checks. PTEN loss is accepted as a moderate stronger-dependency association with specificity checks, while its context-specific high-quality, adenocarcinoma, and aneuploidy checks remain unresolved. Negative or unsupported results include adenocarcinoma-specific attenuation of SMARCA4 loss after failed validation and clean TP53/KEAP1-intact interaction checks, the media-serum SMARCA4 interaction, STK11 main effect, ARID1A main effect, and multiple research markers or common molecular alterations. Remaining uncertainty concerns technical predictors, remaining broad molecular markers, SMARCA4 specificity against ARID1A loss, STK11-hypoxia follow-up, genomic instability context checks, and PTEN context robustness. The most informative next work is to screen the technical predictors and remaining untested molecular markers, then revisit only those context checks that may alter interpretation of the accepted core. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, biological mechanism, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Round 4 synthesis notes. Signed convention: direction -1 positive = stronger/more negative dependency; direction +1 positive = weaker/less negative dependency. Main updates: H16 PTEN loss accepted and validated in direction -1; point estimates .217 and .251 exceed threshold, but validation lower bound below threshold, so main claim accepted while PTEN context checks remain unresolved. H61 CDKN2A accepted as strict high-quality TP53/KEAP1-intact SMARCA4-intact subgroup association; R47 .172 [0.085,0.259], R53 .184 [0.060,0.308]; effect direction replicated but interval still includes subthreshold values, so accepted with caution and not as overall CDKN2A. H19 overall CDKN2A rejected/closed because point estimate .144 is below threshold and high-quality overall H46 .130 also below threshold. Supported core: SMARCA4 loss strong stronger-dependency association validated and robust across TP53-intact/KEAP1-intact, TP53-loss/KEAP1-loss, adenocarcinoma, and high-hypoxia contexts. TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss are accepted weaker-dependency associations, validated or high-quality and robust in several co-occurrence/stemness contexts. PTEN loss is accepted moderate stronger-dependency association with marker-specific checks; contexts unresolved. Negative/closed: adenocarcinoma attenuation unsupported, media interaction null, STK11 main null, ARID1A main null, research markers null, Kras/Pik3ca/Smad4/Rb1/Mtap nulls. Active uncertainty: technical predictors H38/H39/H76, broad molecular H53-H55 and H65-H68, SMARCA4 specificity H21/H28/H77, STK11-hypoxia H27/H64, genomic instability contexts H35/H36/H37/H62/H63, PTEN context checks H40/H41/H43/H44/H69/H75. Next: prioritize broad technical and molecular screens and existing untested accepted-core context checks; avoid further PTEN/CDKN2A validation until technical confounders are assessed. All claims are dataset-specific associations."
